{"sections":[],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"HeadwireCapture"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"The capture pipeline"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CapturePipeline"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every call into the capture session runs on one serial queue, owned by an actor whose executor is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that queue, so ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"startRunning"},{"text":", which blocks until frames flow, never runs on the main thread. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"app drives it through ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"; this article follows one card through that client’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"endpoints.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Finding the card","anchor":"Finding-the-card","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/devices","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" streams the connected external video devices. It observes the discovery","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"session’s device list, which the system updates on every plug and unplug, so there is no polling","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and no fixed delay; repeated lists are dropped. A card can show up before its format list is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"filled in, so ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/start","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" polls for the formats, every 250 ms for up to about two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"seconds, and goes on as soon as they appear.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Choosing the format","anchor":"Choosing-the-format","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/formats","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" returns the formats a device offers, in the order it lists them. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"first time the app opens a card, before it sets a format, it records the card’s own active format","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and frame duration as a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CardPreferredMode"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/start","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" then resolves the format with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FormatSelection.resolve(_:in:cardPrefers:)"},{"text":": the person’s selection where the card offers it,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"else the preferred format, which tries the card’s own mode first and otherwise favours frame rate,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"at least 1080p, uncompressed over compressed, and 16:9. The same resolver tells Settings which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"format Automatic picked, so the sheet and the stream agree.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The session uses the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".inputPriority"},{"text":" preset, so the device’s active format is the one applied.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The minimum and maximum frame durations are both pinned to the rate’s exact duration, 1001\/60000","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for 59.94 fps, rather than one computed from a rounded rate.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Reading the frames","anchor":"Reading-the-frames","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The session has one video data output, beside the preview layer rather than in front of it. It","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hands each frame in turn to three consumers: the Metal presenter, the content sampler, and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"calibration recorder. Uncompressed formats arrive as the card sends them, with nothing converted.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"For a codec, the output asks the system to decode, preferring biplanar 4:2:0; where the output","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"offers no uncompressed format, the app decodes Motion JPEG, H.264, or HEVC itself. Late frames are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"discarded rather than queued.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The content sampler reads one frame on each format change and then one every two seconds, on a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"queue of its own. Each read finds where the Mac’s picture sits inside a padded frame","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/contentBounds","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"), whether the frames carry the range their pixel format claims","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/rangeReadings","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"), and what the frame looks like (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/frameLooks","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"),","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which the app uses to tell a live picture from a no-signal field. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/recordCalibration","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"copies a small crop of every frame for the length of one calibration.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The output also counts the frames that arrive. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/deliveredFrameRate","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" reports the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rate over the last second. When two meter windows in a row deliver under 90% of the rate the card","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"was set to, and the format was chosen automatically, the session restarts once on another pixel","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"format at the same resolution and rate, skipping a format that differs only in colour range. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"format the person chose in Settings is kept.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Drawing the picture","anchor":"Drawing-the-picture","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CapturePreviewView","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" shows the stream. With upscaling off, the session’s own preview layer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"draws it and no frame passes through the app. The Metal path takes over for an upscaler (MetalFX,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or super resolution finished with MetalFX), for a colour correction the card’s profile calls for,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and for a codec the app decodes. It converts each frame on the GPU the moment it arrives and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"presents it straight away, with no display link. If the GPU stages cannot be built, or a frame","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"arrives in a layout the shader cannot read, the view falls back to the preview layer.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/FrameFeed","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" puts frames from outside a capture session, such as a decoded network stream,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"through the same Metal path, so scaling, the reported layout, and upscaling behave as they do for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a card.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"When the session stops","anchor":"When-the-session-stops","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Session notifications are reduced to one ordered stream of events. An interruption is reported as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CaptureSessionState.interrupted(device:reason:)"},{"text":" and its end as running again. A runtime error","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or the card being unplugged tears the session down and reports a failure. After a media services","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reset the session restarts the last request from scratch, up to three times a minute; past that it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fails and the person is asked to replug the card.","type":"text"}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/headwirecapture\/capturepipeline"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How a capture card goes from plugged in to on screen."}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Essentials","title":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient"]}],"references":{"doc://headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture/documentation/HeadwireCapture":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/headwirecapture","abstract":[{"text":"External capture on iPadOS: finding a USB capture card, running it in a chosen format, and showing its video full screen.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture","title":"HeadwireCapture"},"doc://headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture/documentation/HeadwireCapture/CaptureClient/deliveredFrameRate":{"abstract":[{"text":"The rate frames arrived at over the last second, emitted now and each second while frames flow.","type":"text"}],"title":"deliveredFrameRate","identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/deliveredFrameRate","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/headwirecapture\/captureclient\/deliveredframerate","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"deliveredFrameRate","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"@Sendable","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" () -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsyncStream","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?>","kind":"text"}]},"doc://headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture/documentation/HeadwireCapture/CaptureClient/recordCalibration":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"recordCalibration"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"attribute","text":"@Sendable"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"_"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"crop"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"CalibrationGeometry","preciseIdentifier":"s:20HeadwireCaptureModel19CalibrationGeometryV"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Crop","preciseIdentifier":"s:20HeadwireCaptureModel19CalibrationGeometryV4CropV"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"_"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"duration"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Duration","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"CalibrationRecording","preciseIdentifier":"s:20HeadwireCaptureModel20CalibrationRecordingV"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/recordCalibration","title":"recordCalibration","deprecated":true,"url":"\/documentation\/headwirecapture\/captureclient\/recordcalibration","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Copies ","type":"text"},{"code":"crop","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" out of every frame for ","type":"text"},{"code":"duration","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", for a calibration, and returns the copies.","type":"text"}]},"doc://headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture/documentation/HeadwireCapture/CaptureClient/frameLooks":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"frameLooks","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"@Sendable","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" () -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsyncStream","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"FrameLook","preciseIdentifier":"s:20HeadwireCaptureModel9FrameLookV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?>","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/frameLooks","title":"frameLooks","url":"\/documentation\/headwirecapture\/captureclient\/framelooks","abstract":[{"text":"The look of each frame the content sampler reads, about every two seconds while frames flow.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture/documentation/HeadwireCapture/CaptureClient/rangeReadings":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"rangeReadings"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"attribute","text":"@Sendable"},{"kind":"text","text":" () -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:ScS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"AsyncStream"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:20HeadwireCaptureModel12RangeReadingO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"RangeReading"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/rangeReadings","title":"rangeReadings","url":"\/documentation\/headwirecapture\/captureclient\/rangereadings","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What the stream’s frames say about their pixel format’s range label, emitted now and on every change."}]},"doc://headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture/documentation/HeadwireCapture/CaptureClient":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"CaptureClient"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient","title":"CaptureClient","url":"\/documentation\/headwirecapture\/captureclient","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Discovers external capture devices and streams one of them to a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CapturePreviewView"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"CaptureClient"}]},"doc://headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture/documentation/HeadwireCapture/CaptureClient/contentBounds":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where the source’s picture sits inside the padded frame, emitted now and again on every change."}],"title":"contentBounds","identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/contentBounds","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/headwirecapture\/captureclient\/contentbounds","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"contentBounds","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"text":"@Sendable","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" () -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsyncStream","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScS"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"ContentBounds","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:20HeadwireCaptureModel13ContentBoundsV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?>"}]},"doc://headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture/documentation/HeadwireCapture/CapturePreviewView":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Shows the capture stream at a scaling and reports where the video and its content land."}],"title":"CapturePreviewView","identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CapturePreviewView","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"CapturePreviewView"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/headwirecapture\/capturepreviewview","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"CapturePreviewView"}]},"doc://headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture/documentation/HeadwireCapture/CaptureClient/start":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"start"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"attribute","text":"@Sendable"},{"text":" (","kind":"